{
  "case_id": "2005-04-1371",
  "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d6d37546a34-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What about the --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d6d37546a34-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Your Honor, that was an accurate description of the state of the law, as it existed at the time, at least in theory, although, as a practical matter, Respondents have not been able to point to a single reported case a -- of a holder class action in State court prior to the adoption of the Uniform Standards Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d6d37546a34-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And with respect to Blue Chip, Your Honor, it's important to remember what Blue Chip was doing. Blue Chip was not a case about the scope of the \"in connection with\" requirement or the section 10(b) prohibition. Instead, it was a case about what to infer about what Congress would have wanted to authorize as an -- as a right of action, if it had addressed the question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d6d37546a34-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position is that SLUSA does not preempt class actions asserting holder claims. Congress incorporated this Court's interpretation of \"in connection with\" from Blue Chip Stamps when it enacted SLUSA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d6d37546a34-0001-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They do not, for private civil-action purposes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d6d37546a34-0001-0011",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What the Court addressed in the Blue Chip Stamps case was a very different kind of case. It involved nonpurchasers."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d6d37546a34-0001-0012",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The holder's claim wouldn't exist, but for purchases and sales that caused the price to go up."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOUTER",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d6d37546a34-0001-0014",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What did Congress intend? And --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice STEVENS",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d6d37546a34-0001-0015",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And are you aware -- you mentioned the 100 years of State precedent -- is there any precedent in the State law for class actions for holder claims?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d6d37546a34-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What is there in the statute that says the two have to go with each other?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Frederick",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d6d37546a34-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The hoops that Congress went to, and which I have articulated, in the congressional findings, are that the particular harm that Congress was addressing in SLUSA -- this was a narrow -- you know, this was a narrowly framed preemption as to Federal-law claims, because a -- the PSLRA only governed Federal-law claims."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d6d37546a34-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One is -- we know about the holder claims. They are saved for State actions. They're not preempted. What else would fall in this category that is not -- that SLUSA doesn't affect, that can be brought as class actions in State court?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer and Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d6d37546a34-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Breyer and Justice Ginsburg asked questions that I think illustrate that Congress could not have intended such an anomalous result by allowing holders' claims to proceed as nonpreempted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3d6d37546a34706f1a084aec0d015512ff6aa17ccf8e93cd5892f22dcc7230c2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3d6d37546a34-0003-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
